DuoLinux - licence notes
========================

1. This project's own work
   (toolkit/, configs/, overlay/, tests/, docs/, out/remote/, out/overlay/,
   out/abl/*.sh, out/patch/, the top-level scripts and README)

   Copyright (c) 2026 the DuoLinux author. All rights reserved until a licence
   is chosen.

   >>> ACTION BEFORE PUBLISHING: pick a licence and replace this section with
   >>> its text. An earlier version of README.md stated "Tooling and overlay:
   >>> MIT"; if that is still the intent, put the MIT licence text here.

2. Third-party code included in this repository (licences unchanged)

   out/wvkbd-0.15/   wvkbd 0.15, modified.
                     Copyright (c) 2020 John Sullivan <jsullivan@csumb.edu>
                     and contributors. GNU GPL v3.0 - see out/wvkbd-0.15/LICENSE
                     and COPYING. os-compatibility.[ch]: MIT/X, see
                     out/wvkbd-0.15/COPYING_WESTON.
                     Modifications: out/wvkbd-0.15/NOTICE.duolinux (GPLv3).

   out/vboard-fork/  Vboard, modified, reference only (not deployed).
                     Copyright (c) 2025 mdev588,
                     Copyright (c) 2026 Archisman Panigrahi.
                     GNU GPL v3.0 - see out/vboard-fork/LICENSE and
                     out/vboard-fork/NOTICE.duolinux.

   Those directories must keep their licence files and copyright notices
   when redistributed. Section 1 does not apply to them.

3. Not included

   The Linux kernel (GPL-2.0), firmware blobs, openABL, InputPlumber and
   Debian packages are fetched from their upstreams at build or install time
   and are not redistributed in this repository.
